    "title": "Let It Be (The Replacements album)",
    "description": "1984 album by the Replacements",
    "extract": "Let It Be is the third studio album by American rock band the Replacements. It was released on October 2, 1984, by Twin/Tone Records. A post-punk album with coming-of-age themes, Let It Be was recorded by the band after they had grown tired of playing loud and fast exclusively as on their 1983 Hootenanny album; the group decided to write songs that were, according to vocalist Paul Westerberg, \"a little more sincere.\"",
